eeing the flop cheaply while preserving chips. Raising or all-in with this hand is too aggressive and lacks sufficient equity. Folding avoids immediate loss but misses pot-building opportunities.\n\nReason: K7o has moderate pre-flop equity but is out of position against a raise. Calling 200 maintains pot control and allows post-flop decisions based on community cards. Aggressive action (raise/all-in) risks overcommitting with a weak hand, while folding discards potential equity. Given the large chip stack, a call is both safe and strategic.\n\nAnswer: 200"}
